  "privacyReportScreenExplanation": "Trareon Transcribe makes no network calls at all while transcribing, whether recording live or importing a file. Audio never leaves this device.\n\nThere are four legitimate kinds of network activity, and you start all of them yourself:\n1. Whisper model download: from huggingface.co, only when you choose a model that isn't on this device yet.\n2. AI summary: sends the transcript text (not the audio) to an endpoint you set yourself. This feature is off by default and points to Ollama on this computer (localhost) by default, so even the default never leaves the device.\n3. Update check: fetches a single version file from raw.githubusercontent.com when you press \"Check for updates\". Nothing is downloaded or run automatically.\n4. \"View release\": opens the releases page in your browser.\n\nAll four are recorded in the log above, along with where they went. Every place in the code that can start one of them must record itself first, and this is tested automatically (test/privacy_proof_test.dart).",
